From a30a69abb3e0ad3cd5348952a2c4be101e7d1a09 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 05:21:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02274/11362] [outer-loop] autolearning: capture successful
 gap-fills + reuse them pre-generated

Per operator: successful dynamically-generated gap-fills are rolled back in for future runs.
- gap_fills/ package: save_heuristic / load_heuristic / captured_games -- persists a per-game
  goal_distance heuristic as committed code (bundle-able for the offline competition).
- arc_gap_fill.py: REUSE-FIRST (load_heuristic -> skip the LLM if already captured, deterministic
  + instant); SAVE-ON-SUCCESS (only after the heuristic HELPED the search solve, reproduction-
  gated -> trustworthy by construction).
- generate() gains a  callback -> rejects runtime-buggy code (cn04's 12B heuristic
  returned None) and retries. Each captured gap-fill compounds; the system gets faster per game.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
